     1	"""BC-centering: fine-tune the DiT (last layers) to CENTER the target — the Stage-3 de-risk.
     2	
     3	Diagnosis (memory acot-uav-reid-reframe): the deployable SR gap is the DiT framing the target
     4	OFF-center (decorrelate design) → reid degrades → cascade. frame-gain (fixed geometric gain,
     5	either sign) fails: too weak to move the DiT + amplifies reid errors. So the fix must be a
     6	LEARNED, in-DiT centering. This script BC-fine-tunes the DiT (flow-matching, last layers only,
     7	VLM/EAR/IAR frozen) toward a CENTERING action target — teaching the DiT to output actions that
     8	point the camera at the (z_ex-indicated) target.
     9	
    10	Centering target (validated: corr(off, yaw_err)=+0.677, sign +off=toward-target):
    11	  a1[k] = [recorded dx,dy,dz at i+k ; dyaw_center[k] ; recorded search]
    12	  dyaw_center[k] = clip(yaw_err(target[i+k], cam[i+k]), ±cap) / a_scale
    13	DECOUPLES the decorrelate tension: off-center TRAINING DATA stays (VLM/reid features frozen,
    14	identity load-bearing); only the DiT CONTROL is fine-tuned to center → does NOT re-introduce
    15	the shortcut. z_ex during training = CV of the TRUE target (so the DiT learns "center what z_ex
    16	points at"); at inference z_ex = reid-committed target.
