 succeeded in 6ms:
     1	"""Stage 0 — LoRA on Qwen3-VL so the layer-24 representation carries WHICH (language-specified target among
     2	look-alikes). OFFLINE, on recorded mvp_full_v5 episodes; supervised by GT identity (training-time privilege only).
     3	
     4	Model: Qwen3-VL-4B (bf16), text-before-image prompt with the neutralized instruction (same as the deployed
     5	encoder, acot_probe/backbones.py::Qwen3VLBackbone.encode). Forward runs only the first 24 decoder layers; the
     6	readout = output of decoder layer 23 (0-based) == hidden_states[24] of the full model (pre-norm). LoRA on the
     7	attention projections of layers [lora_lo, 23] (the layers feeding the readout). Candidate features = mean-pool
     8	of the image-token grid inside each GT-projected candidate box (same boxes as the closed-loop harness).
     9	Head: per-candidate score = MLP(LN(cand)) + bilinear(LN(cand), LN(text_mean)); CE over in-frame candidates.
    10	rank 0 = frozen-Qwen linear/MLP probe (the baseline that isolates what LoRA adds).
    11	
    12	Eval (val/test from train/splits/mvp_full_split.json, episodes on disk only): per-frame pick accuracy over
    13	target-present frames with >=2 candidates; subsets: look-alike frames (a `similar` distractor in frame),
    14	unseen target description (not in train); language-swap control (instruction replaced by another episode's
    15	target description → should fall toward chance if the model uses language).
    16	  python train/qwen_lora_grounding.py --rank 16 --out runs/qwen_lora/r16
    17	  python train/qwen_lora_grounding.py --rank 0  --out runs/qwen_lora/r0
    18	"""
    19	from __future__ import annotations
    20	
    21	import argparse
    22	import glob
    23	import json
