     1	"""ASD module — drift correction for closed-loop self-updating identity memories.
     2	
     3	MAIN METHOD (mode="filter", filter_kind="tempered") = PGIF, Posterior-Gated Identity Filtering:
     4	  a memory-agnostic wrapper around ANY identity memory that (i) picks a candidate, (ii) reports a confidence on any
     5	  scale, (iii) exposes an update hook. Per decision tick it keeps a tempered, confidence-weighted evidence count per
     6	  persistent tracklet  L_k <- lam*L_k + (0.5 + rank(conf))*1[k = memory pick]  and, when argmax_k L_k disagrees with
     7	  the memory's pick, re-does the memory update with the argmax crop and commits control to it (posterior gating).
     8	  Rationale (acot_note/1001_innovation-design.md): self-update makes the memory's errors autocorrelated, so evidence
     9	  must be tempered (untempered Bayes = ablation, gets captured); gating stops wrong picks being written into memory.
    10	ABLATIONS: filter_kind="resid" (equal weights), "bayes" (untempered sticky HMM), gate_memory=False (commit-only).
    11	LEGACY (negative results, kept for reproducibility): modes "rule"/"learned" = frozen appearance+language anchor with
    12	  multi-hypothesis CUSUM; "observe" = log statistics only (no intervention).
    13	GT is never used at decision time; `true_slot` is only written to the log for offline scoring."""
