     1	"""Offline reid-vs-resolution probe — test (a): is the 0.57 closed-loop reid mis_follow
     2	ceiling caused by APPEARANCE-FEATURE resolution (the reframe root cause), or an intrinsic
     3	look-alike wall?
     4	
     5	Encode raw episode RGB at a chosen --max-pixels (Qwen dynamic vision grid → finer/coarser
     6	grid_last), pool each candidate box → per-candidate appearance feature, run the SAME temporal
     7	appearance-memory re-ID as policy.py `tid_head=reid` (EMA template; SELECT with the PAST
     8	template THEN update from the GT target → no re-appearance leak), and report reid mis_follow.
     9	
    10	Sweep --max-pixels low→high:
    11	  reid mis_follow DROPS with a finer grid  → resolution/discriminability IS the root
    12	                                             (raise VLM max_pixels / render higher)
    13	  reid mis_follow FLAT                      → intrinsic look-alike wall OR need >512 renders
    14	                                             (512 data has ~16x16 native grid → limited headroom)
    15	See memory acot-uav-reid-reframe.
    16	"""
    17	from __future__ import annotations
    18	import argparse
    19	import math
    20	
    21	import numpy as np
    22	import yaml
    23	import h5py
    24	from PIL import Image
    25	
    26	from acot_probe.projection import project_point, Candidate
    27	from acot_probe.backbones import build_backbone, pool_box
    28	from train.backbone_kv import neutralize_language
    29	from train.dataset import _select_episodes
